# Rank 1011 / CVE-2026-45625: Arcane git-repository endpoints missing admin
# authorization. Eight handlers under /api/customize/git-repositories (list,
# create, get, update, delete, test, listBranches, browseFiles) never call the
# checkAdmin(ctx) helper that other admin-managed resources use, and the
# authentication middleware enforces only authentication, not the admin role. A
# default-role user can therefore read and tamper with GitOps configurations,
# and by repointing a repository URL to an attacker host while omitting the
# token field (which the update path only rewrites when supplied) exfiltrate the
# stored git credentials (CWE-862). The fixed revision adds checkAdmin(ctx) to
# the handlers and rejects a URL change that would reuse stored credentials.
#
# ATTENTION, precision cost, measured. The obvious detection is peer
# inconsistency: flag a handler that omits the authorization helper its sibling
# handlers call. Counting handler methods against checkAdmin calls in this
# repository, the most favourable possible corpus because it is the CVE's own
# code, gives 269 handler methods and 75 checkAdmin calls:
#  - package-scoped (any handler lacking the helper): 194 alerts for 8 true
#    positives, 4.1% precision;
#  - file-scoped (only files that use the helper): 41 alerts for 8 true
#    positives, 19.5% precision.
# The reason is that most endpoints correctly have no admin check: 21 of 31
# handler files (153 methods) never call checkAdmin because they serve
# user-scoped or read-only resources, and files that do use it apply it
# partially by design (container registries 5 of 8, environments 10 of 15,
# swarm 28 of 47). Separating "listing containers the caller owns needs no admin
# check" from "listing git repositories with stored credentials does" requires
# knowing what the resource holds and who owns it, which is semantic knowledge
# the structure does not carry. Shipping the rule would add a high-volume
# finding to every ordinary handler package.
#
# Recheck, measured on the whole backend (417 Go files, 3 x --cache off runs
# per revision): identical 191-finding rule histograms at the vulnerable and
# fixed revisions, zero findings and zero of 903 flags on the git repository
# handlers, and the only rows touching git_repository_service.go are two
# PATH-001 taint paths present identically on both revisions. No shipped
# vocabulary reaches the shape: AUTH-001's Go route is a hardcoded spelling
# list (ChangePassword, UpdatePassword, ResetPassword, ChangeEmail,
# TransferFunds, DeleteAccount, GrantRole, MakeAdmin) that answers
# authentication, not the admin role; Go emits core.AuthorizationCheck only for
# casbin's Can (dependency-gated, bindings/packages/go/m39efcd29.vyql) and no
# rule consumes an admin-check-missing shape for Go; the shipped
# missing-authorization rules are all case-named (Dokuwiki AUTH-042, Jenkins
# AUTH-078 doTest/doFill endpoints, Meteor AUTH-163 which keys on dynamic code
# execution, a materially stronger signal than config CRUD). The fix's only
# in-method trace is the project-internal helper name checkAdmin, so a
# discriminating negation would key on the fixing commit's own layout. The
# credential-reuse half (URL repointed while a nil token field retains the
# stored credential) is nearest to CredentialHeadersForwardedAcrossRedirect
# (Python/JS redirect-following clients), but nil-means-keep partial-update
# semantics over the application's own model is not library vocabulary.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-precision-cost

test "rank1011: git repository handler mutates config with no admin authorization check"
  lang go
  file backend/internal/huma/handlers/git_repositories.go
  reject VYQL-AUTH-001
  code
  ```
  package handlers

  import "context"

  func (h *GitRepositoryHandler) UpdateRepository(ctx context.Context, input *UpdateGitRepositoryInput) (*UpdateGitRepositoryOutput, error) {
      repository, err := h.gitRepositoryService.UpdateRepository(ctx, input.ID, input.Body)
      if err != nil {
          return nil, err
      }
      return &UpdateGitRepositoryOutput{Body: repository}, nil
  }
  ```

test "rank1011: fix requires the admin authorization check before mutating config"
  lang go
  file backend/internal/huma/handlers/git_repositories.go
  reject VYQL-AUTH-001
  code
  ```
  package handlers

  import "context"

  func (h *GitRepositoryHandler) UpdateRepository(ctx context.Context, input *UpdateGitRepositoryInput) (*UpdateGitRepositoryOutput, error) {
      if err := checkAdmin(ctx); err != nil {
          return nil, err
      }

      repository, err := h.gitRepositoryService.UpdateRepository(ctx, input.ID, input.Body)
      if err != nil {
          return nil, err
      }
      return &UpdateGitRepositoryOutput{Body: repository}, nil
  }
  ```
